  "note": "The Syriac verb ܢܩܦ means to adhere or follow (SEDRA lexeme 2027; Acts 8:13). Its relationship to making a circuit is uncertain. The Hebrew striking verb has its own entry.\n\nThe striking and encircling verbs have identical written forms. The object and the action in each passage guide the choice between them.\n\nMerged from `naqaph`, `naqaph-strike` on 2026-11-20: one root, one entry."
